<title>JAPAN: Joban Kosan to buy back shares for stock options.</title>
<headline>Joban Kosan to buy back shares for stock options.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Resort hotel Joban Kosan Co Ltd said on Tuesday that it would spend up to 45 million yen to buy back up to 10,000 of its shares in order to introduce a stock option scheme.</p>
<p>Stock options give holders the right to buy shares at a set price within a certain period.</p>
<p>In May, Japan changed its law to allow firms to buy back up to 10 percent of their own shares for use in stock option schemes for employees and executives.</p>
<p>Japanese business leaders have said that the system would be effective in motivating employees to work hard.</p>
</text>
